---@field max_tier number The highest tier there is, so the current tier can be shown as progress.
---@field emails_per_day number How many emails this tier allows per day.
---@field max_batch_audience number The largest audience this tier allows for a single batch send.
---@field emails_sent_last_day number Emails sent by this project's workflows in the last 24 hours.
---@field enforced boolean True when these allowances are applied to sends. False while they are only being measured.

---Bounce/complaint rates over the last 30 days of workflow email, computed on the fly from app metrics.
---@class posthog.hog_flows.EmailSendingRates
---@field bounce_rate number Hard (permanent) bounces / emails sent over the last 30 days (0-1), matching how AWS counts its bounce rate — transient bounces (greylisting, mailbox full) are excluded. Bounces are counted when the feedback arrives, so the ratio is approximate at the window boundary and capped at 1.
---@field complaint_rate number Spam complaints / emails sent over the last 30 days (0-1). Complaints are counted when the feedback arrives, so the ratio is approximate at the window boundary and capped at 1.
---@field emails_sent number Emails sent in the last 30 days.

