---@class posthog.hog_flows.HogFlowBatchJob
---@field id string ID of the batch run.
---@field status? posthog.hog_flows.HogFlowBatchJobStateEnum Status of the batch run. waiting: the audience's cohort is still calculating. queued and active: the run is enrolling its audience. completed: the whole audience was enrolled. When every enrolled person's run has ended, or a day after the run completed, PostHog checks for errored sends. A completed run stays completed when no send errored, becomes partially_failed when some sends errored, and becomes failed when every send errored. failed also means the run could not enroll its audience. cancelled: someone stopped the run. A send errors when its step throws, for example on a template that does not render. Provider failures such as bounces are not errored sends; read them from the run's metrics. * `waiting` - Waiting * `queued` - Queued * `active` - Active * `completed` - Completed * `partially_failed` - Partially failed * `cancelled` - Cancelled * `failed` - Failed
---@field hog_flow string ID of the workflow this batch run belongs to.
---@field filters any Audience snapshot the run fanned out to, taken from the workflow's batch trigger filters.
---@field variables? any Variable value overrides applied to this run.
---@field created_at string When the batch run was created.
---@field created_by posthog.hog_flows.UserBasic User who started the batch run.
---@field updated_at string When the batch run was last updated.

---Response from the batch job cancel endpoint. Stopping is asynchronous: this call flags the
---run's audience fan-out and its in-flight child runs, and the workflow workers terminate
---them shortly after. Messages already sent are not recalled.
---@class posthog.hog_flows.HogFlowBatchJobCancelResponse
---@field status posthog.hog_flows.HogFlowBatchJobStateEnum The batch run's status after this request. 'cancelled' once every in-flight run is flagged; a completion that raced the stop wins and is reported instead. * `waiting` - Waiting * `queued` - Queued * `active` - Active * `completed` - Completed * `partially_failed` - Partially failed * `cancelled` - Cancelled * `failed` - Failed
---@field marked number In-flight runs newly flagged for cancellation by this request.
---@field remaining number In-flight runs of this batch not yet flagged. Non-zero on very large runs; call again.
---@field done boolean True when no in-flight runs of this batch remain unflagged.

---* `waiting` - Waiting
---* `queued` - Queued
---* `active` - Active
---* `completed` - Completed
---* `partially_failed` - Partially failed
