---Filter shape for the rerun endpoint. `window_start`/`window_end` are required.
---@class posthog.hog_flows.HogInvocationRerunFilter
---@field window_start string Inclusive lower bound on `scheduled_at` (UTC).
---@field window_end string Exclusive upper bound on `scheduled_at` (UTC).
---@field status? posthog.hog_flows.HogInvocationRerunFilterStatusList Restrict to invocations whose latest status is one of these. Defaults to ['failed'].
---@field error_kind? posthog.hog_flows.HogInvocationRerunFilterErrorKindList Restrict to invocations whose error_kind matches one of these (e.g. 'http_5xx', 'timeout').
---@field error_message_contains? string Restrict to invocations whose error_message contains this substring (case-insensitive). Use to isolate one failure mode when error_kind is too coarse (most app-level errors share the 'hog_error' kind).
---@field max_attempts? number Skip invocations that have already been attempted this many times or more.
---@field max_count? number Maximum number of invocations to rerun in this request. Server-side cap is 10000.
---@field invocation_ids? posthog.hog_flows.HogInvocationRerunFilterInvocationIdsList Optional restriction to specific invocation IDs within the window. Capped at 10000 per request. Always combined with `window_start`/`window_end` so the ClickHouse query can be partition-pruned.

