---@class posthog.hog_flows.ListHogFlowsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field broadcast_eligible? boolean Pass `true` to return broadcasts plus the ordinary workflows the broadcasts UI can render: a batch trigger and a single email step.
---@field broadcast_status? string Comma-separated broadcast statuses as the broadcasts UI shows them: draft, scheduled, sending, sent, partially_sent, failed, archived. Scheduled, sending, sent, partially_sent and failed come from the latest run and whether a schedule still has sends to come. A latest run that is completed reads as sent, partially_failed as partially_sent, and failed or cancelled as failed. With a schedule still to come, a completed or partially_failed latest run reads as scheduled.
---@field created_at? string
---@field created_by? string Filter to workflows created by the user with this uuid.
---@field id? string
---@field latest_send_first? boolean Pass `true` to order by when each workflow's newest completed or partially_failed run finished, newest first. Workflows that never finished such a run come last.
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field name? string Only workflows whose name contains this text, ignoring case. Unlike `search`, it never reads descriptions, tags or step content.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field optimization_enabled? boolean Only workflows someone turned suggestions on for.
---@field origin_product? posthog.hog_flows.ListHogFlowsRequestOriginProduct|string Filter to workflows owned by a product surface, e.g. `loops` for Desktop loops.
---@field search? string Case-insensitive search. Matches workflow name, description and tag names first; only when nothing matches those, it matches step names and the subject line, preheader and body text of email steps, in both the live workflow and its pending draft.
---@field source_record? string Filter to workflows started from this record, as '<kind>:<id>', e.g. `early_access:<id>`.
---@field status? posthog.hog_flows.ListHogFlowsRequestStatus|string * `draft` - Draft * `active` - Active * `archived` - Archived
---@field tags? string JSON-encoded list of tag names, e.g. ["growth", "onboarding"]. Returns workflows that carry at least one of these tags.
---@field trigger? string Filter by trigger config as a JSON object. Returns workflows whose trigger contains the given object, e.g. {"type": "event"}.
---@field type? string Comma-separated workflow types. `loop` and `broadcast` return the workflows those surfaces own; `messaging` returns the remaining workflows with an email, SMS, or push action, and `automation` the rest.
---@field updated_at? string

---@alias posthog.hog_flows.ListHogFlowsRequestOriginProduct "broadcasts"|"loops"|"transactional_emails"

---@alias posthog.hog_flows.ListHogFlowsRequestStatus "active"|"archived"|"draft"

